Date: Mon, 22 Jun 2026 14:02:01 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03464/11362] [conductor] PHASE B2 (RESERVED INFRA) --
 TAUTOLOGY null-delta false-flag guard in adversarial_verify.py: an artifact
 declaring an EXPLICIT null-delta (a *_delta field == 0) WITH a
 null_delta_methodology_note AND a passing positive control is a DECLARED
 honest null, NOT a bug -- downgrade its two-equal-metrics TAUTOLOGY from
 CRITICAL to annotated-WARN so the capstone READS it instead of EXCLUDING it
 (the recurring .423 A3/A4/A6 false-exclusion: with_X=baseline=0.04 tripped
 CRITICAL TAUTOLOGY). Keep TAUTOLOGY CRITICAL for genuinely-distinct-metric
 bit-identity with no declared null-delta. Asserting tests.

Automated research step by research conductor.
Task ID: exp4599-b2

Co-Authored-By: Codex CLI <noreply@openai.com>
